The woman says: "May I see your passport?"
"Yes, of course," I say.
I have my passport in my bag.
I find it and give it to her.
She takes the passport.
She opens it and looks.
She looks at my name and my photo.
Then she looks at the date.
"Ah, your birthday," she says and smiles.
She also looks at my other papers.
"You have all the papers," she says.
She nods slowly.
"That is good."
"Everything is in order."
